# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Studio configuration.  Copy to `.env` and edit.  Everything here is OPTIONAL:
# with no .env at all the studio boots and you set the endpoints in Settings.
#
# NOTHING SECRET GOES IN THIS FILE.  Every VITE_ variable is compiled into the
# JavaScript bundle and served to every visitor, so a key placed here is
# published rather than configured.  The API key is entered in the in-app
# Settings panel and stored in your browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Safe defaults — change only if you self-host the API ──────────────────────

# Where the /v1 API lives. Only the `alakazam` (hosted) provider uses this —
# every other provider ignores it, and the studio runs without it.
#
# LEAVE THESE COMMENTED unless you actually self-host the API. Copying this file
# to .env as-is used to bake http://localhost:8787 into the built bundle, and
# nothing in this repository listens there: `docker compose` serves the studio
# on 4321 and there is no API service in it. The result was a hosted provider
# pointed at a dead port, with the address compiled in rather than settable.
#
#   hosted:  https://api.alakazam.gg   (the default when this is unset)
#   self-hosted: wherever your own /v1 lives
# VITE_ALAKAZAM_API_BASE=https://api.alakazam.gg

# Where the player iframe is served from. Same rule.
#   hosted:  https://play.alakazam.gg   (the default when this is unset)
# VITE_ALAKAZAM_EMBED_HOST=https://play.alakazam.gg

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STILL — the deployed demo's SERVERLESS env (Vercel → Settings → Environment
# Variables). These are read at RUNTIME by /api/* functions, never compiled
# into the bundle; the three of them are the whole runtime surface.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# World models — sessions open from the player's browser straight to Reactor.
REACTOR_API_KEY=

# Ellen's voice — called server-side by /api/voice; never reaches the browser.
FISH_AUDIO_API_KEY=

# The improvised homecoming lines only (a few short calls per playthrough) —
# proxied by /api/llm so the browser never sees this key either.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
